# Quick manual API checks. In Visual Studio / VS Code (REST Client), click "Send Request".
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### Health
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Create a class -> 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/classes
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Class 6 - Morning Shift", "totalSeats": 120 }

### Same name again (case/space-insensitive) -> 409 CLASS_NAME_TAKEN
POST {{baseUrl}}/classes
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "  class 6 -  morning shift ", "totalSeats": 50 }

### Invalid body -> 400 VALIDATION_FAILED
POST {{baseUrl}}/classes
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "", "totalSeats": 0 }

### Wrong type -> 400 VALIDATION_FAILED
POST {{baseUrl}}/classes
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Class 7 - Day Shift", "totalSeats": "many" }

### List classes with seat counts -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/classes

### One class (paste an id from the list) -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/classes/c_replace_me

### Unknown class -> 404 CLASS_NOT_FOUND
GET {{baseUrl}}/classes/c_does_not_exist
